      "content": "but the juice i had earlier didnt really work and i'm still feeling super shaky... i'm just so worried about a massive spike later. if i take like 1.5 units of my fast acting insulin right now, won't that act as a buffer so it doesn't swing too crazy? it feels like a more controlled way to handle it rather than just eating a bunch of sugar and hoping for the best. wouldn't a tiny bit of insulin actually help stabilize the levels in the long run?",
